From: MGS2 RG353VS compatibility port
Subject: [PATCH] libdg: retain the patch fixed-function renderer on DXVK/Mali

The original hardware-vertex-processing branch enables the custom wpatch
vertex shader unconditionally.  That shader produces no sea surface through
the D3D8 -> DXVK-Sarek -> Mali route, while libdg's existing non-shader wpatch
path renders and animates the same surface correctly.

The distributed 2003 executable is not stored in this repository.  The
corresponding fail-closed runtime patch changes the immediate operand of this
single flag set at file offset 0x4a294a from 0x02 to 0x00.  No other byte is
changed.

--- a/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/wdgd.c
+++ b/mgs2x/source/system/libdg/wdgd.c
@@ -1459,7 +1459,6 @@
 			}
 			DG_WinApp.flag |= M_DG_WINAPP_SHADOWWT_USE_VERTEXSHADER ;
 			DG_WinApp.flag |= M_DG_WINAPP_OPTCMF00_USE_VERTEXSHADER ;
-			DG_WinApp.flag |= M_DG_WINAPP_PATCH_USE_VERTEXSHADER ;
 
 			/* DG_EVMOBJ描画VertexShader使用判定  */
 			if(  X2W_GetAppConfig(X2WAPPCFG_EVM_USE_OBJ_MULTITEX) )
